# Deployment

## Infrastructure

In the repo, we have a [terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform) file (`main.tf`)
to set up the infrastructure for the app using AWS.

Here's a diagram that outlines the configured infrastructure:

![Diagram of project infrastructure](<%= image_path('docs/infrastructure.png') %>)

### Setting up

To start, you need to install and configure the aws cli with your AWS credentials.
We recommend creating a profile specifically for this project to avoid conflicts with other AWS
projects you may have.
You can do this by running the following command:

```bash
aws configure --profile <your-profile-name>
```

Also, you'll need to create an SSH key pair to connect to your EC2 instance.

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C <user-address>
```

Once you have your profile set up, add a `secret.tfvars` file with the following variables:

```hcl
deployer_key     = "ssh-ed25519 abc user@test.com" # SSH public key
app_name         = "my-app" # Name of the app, used for naming resources in AWS, must not have spaces or underscores
rails_master_key = "123456" # Rails master key for credentials
db_password      = "123456" # Database password
dns_name         = "my-app.com" # Name of the hosted zone on Route 53. You must create this hosted zone in advance.
site_url         = "template.eagerworks.com" # URL of the site
aws_profile      = "<your-profile-name>" # AWS profile name you created earlier
```

### Running Terraform

Once you have everything ready, you can run the following
commands to set up the infrastructure:

```bash
terraform init
terraform plan -var-file=secret.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=secret.tfvars
```

This will initialize Terraform, show you the plan of what will be created,
and then apply the changes to create the infrastructure.

## Deployment

For deployment, we are using [kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org).

### Setting up Kamal

Once terraform finishes running, the outputs should have the information you need fill in the
`config/deploy.yml` file.

You will need to set the following values in the `config/deploy.yml` file:

```yaml
image: <app_name>/web-server

service: <app_name>

servers:
  web:
    - &web_server <web server ip>

registry:
  server: 111111111111.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com # Replace with your ECR registry
  password: <%= %x(aws ecr --profile <your-profile-name> get-login-password) %>

ssh:
  proxy: ubuntu@<bastion public ip>
```

Also, make sure to edit the profile name and the bastion public IP address on the files
`.kamal/secrets` and `.kamal/hooks/docker-setup`

Once you have everything set up, you can run the following commands to deploy the app:

```bash
kamal setup # Currently this throws a docker permission error, but you can ignore it
kamal deploy
```
